[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/1657200483","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/106251#issuecomment-1657200483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/106251","id":1657200483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z85ixt9j","user":{"login":"hisushanta","id":93595990,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZQpVg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93595990?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta","html_url":"https://github.com/hisushanta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hisushanta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-30T15:24:26Z","updated_at":"2023-07-30T15:24:26Z","body":"The MultiMarginLoss function in PyTorch calculates the loss between a set of input data and a set of labels. The labels are represented as a tensor, and the input data is defined as another tensor. The two tensors must have the same shape, except for the first dimension. This is because the MultiMarginLoss function uses the first dimension of the labels tensor to determine the number of classes.\r\n\r\nFor example, if the label's tensor has a shape of [8], then there are 8 classes. The input tensor must also have a shape of [8], but the other dimensions can be any size.\r\n\r\n**Code Change:**\r\ntarget_size = [7]\r\nreplace \r\ntarget_size = [8]","author_associatio